 "traps": [
  "every version and most coordinates come from two catalogs: gradle/libs.versions.toml (libs.*) and the Micronaut platform catalog loaded in settings.gradle.kts (mn.*), so mn.micronaut.jooq names a library that no file of the project spells out",
  "the frameworks differ per Gradle project: :app is the Micronaut application, :model a Micronaut library with jOOQ code generation, :shared and :ui have no Micronaut plugin",
  "tests use Kotest on the JUnit Platform (kotest-runner-junit5), not JUnit Jupiter; Playwright exists only in the uiTest source set",
  "htmx, Alpine.js and the Tabler CSS framework are vendored minified files under ui/src/main/resources/public/ext, included by Layout.kt; the HTML is written with kotlinx.html, not a template engine, while Pebble renders e-mail and webhook templates in :app",
  "ui/src/jsTest runs with node --test from a Gradle Exec task: there is no package.json and no JavaScript test framework",
  "docs/ is a separate MkDocs site with its own requirements.txt and no project name, referred to by its root",
  "the notification services (PagerDuty, Pushover, Slack, Telegram, Discord, Microsoft Teams, Apprise, SMTP) are named only by the integration classes and their URLs; Keycloak appears only in localdev/docker-compose.yml and in Testcontainers tests",
  "only frameworks and services are measured; the other facets are in unknown"
 ],
